# Indobase production redeploy (Vyom / indobase.in)

Use this **only** when the user asks to ship to **prod**, deploy to **Vyom**, or promote after staging is OK. Day-to-day Studio/Builder work goes to **`staging`** → `indobase.fun` first (see `staging-first-deploy.mdc`).

## 1. Source of truth

- **Repo branch:** `main` on GitHub (`Indobase/Indobase`) — after promotion from `staging`.
- **CI:** Push to `main` triggers `.github/workflows/docker-publish.yml` → Docker Hub `roshanraghavander/ind-repo:<sha>` and `roshanraghavander/indobase-builder:<sha>`.
- Prefer the **commit SHA** tag for rollout (not `:latest`).

## 2. Git (promotion)

- Confirm staging was validated on `studio.indobase.fun` / `builder.indobase.fun` (or user opts out).
- Integrate `staging` → `main` as directed, then **`git push origin main`**.
- `SHA=$(git rev-parse HEAD)` on `main` after that push.

## 3. VPS rollout (Docker Swarm)

- **Control-plane:** `root@103.190.92.249` (Studio + Builder + platform Postgres)
- **Tenant data-plane:** `root@103.190.92.248` (provisioner + tenant stacks)
- **SSH key:** `~/.ssh/id_ed25519_indobase_vps`
- **Service:** on `.249`, `docker service ls --format '{{.Name}}' | grep -E 'indobase-studio' | head -1`

1. Wait for Hub tag `roshanraghavander/ind-repo:<SHA>` (and Builder tag) HTTP 200.
2. On `.249`: pull image(s), `docker service update --image …`, run `indobase-studio-attach-compose-network.sh`.
3. Verify: `curl -sS https://studio.indobase.in/api/health/live` → `version` == `<SHA>`.

Do **not** deploy Studio/Builder to Hostinger `187.77.30.165`. Staging Hostinger is `72.61.242.251` (`indobase.fun`) only.

